From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fork contributor <contributor@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:26:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ios: edit the touch controls from the in-game menu (move,
 size, opacity)

Adds Edit control layout to the in-game menu (GameMenu.swift). It opens a layout editor over the
game: drag any control to move it (DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT's steps, kept inside its area and clear of the
others), one size slider for every control, an opacity slider, a switch to move the A B X Y keys
one by one, Reset, Cancel and Done. Done saves the arrangement, the size and the opacity in
NSUserDefaults, so a game's own app, which has no launcher to edit them in, keeps them.
Saved edits are dropped when DM_TOUCH_LAYOUT or DM_TOUCH_SIZE in the environment changes.

DmPadGeometry.h gains dm_pad_layout_encode and dm_pad_control_ref, tested on the Mac in
pad_geometry_check.m.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Let a game's own app (no launcher) edit the touch controls in game: move, size, opacity
Issue: none

